  "limitations": [
    "Synthetic standard GQA/SwiGLU geometry only, not the hybrid Qwen checkpoint. No embeddings/head, checkpoint mapping, GDN, Q/K norms, attention gates, bias, paging or KV quantization.",
    "Two sequential layers, concurrency 1. Fixed-position replay with explicit suffix truncation is not a sustained autoregressive rollout, model TPS or HTTP-serving benchmark.",
    "Dense prefill remains much slower than the explicit PyTorch reference; no fast-backend promotion or general inference-speedup claim.",
    "Q4 compares packed native execution with exact decoded values materialized in FP32 for the PyTorch reference, not another quantized engine. These synthetic Q4 codes are uniform [-8,7], not quantized pretrained weights; their nonzero mean can produce large common-mode activations over two layers. Maximum absolute cross-backend difference 4.0 is retained, not hidden; normalized diagnostics and unchanged per-Op bounds are reported separately. No model-quality or lossless BF16 claim.",
    "Native-vs-reference full-chain results are not bit-identical. All individual Ops pass their independent FP64 bounds on actual represented inputs; each native shared-arena composition/cache exactly matches independently executed native Ops.",
    "Sharing workspace saves activation/scratch bytes, not layer weights or persistent KV. Timing differences between shared/separate workspaces are small; one ABBA session with two samples per condition is not a confidence interval.",
    "Execution process CPU is about one busy core, including Python validation/dispatch/cache bookkeeping and CUDA-event waiting; no idle-CPU optimization.",
    "NVML is whole-device/coarse, sampled every 200 ms after excluding the first second. Both backend residents coexist during the comparison; NVML VRAM is not a minimal single-backend model peak. GPU busy is not achieved occupancy; memory-controller busy is not bandwidth percentage. Hardware counters remain restricted; no new attribution/timeline diagnosis.",
    "Upload owns copies, including if source is already on GPU. It does not automatically adopt/free checkpoint allocations. Weight source lifetimes and releasing redundant source references remain explicit caller responsibilities.",
    "Graph capture supports a fixed token shape and position. It uses a dependency-bridged non-default preparation stream; cache visibility changes only in managed replay, not during capture. Capture requires no other CUDA work/allocations in this process."
  ],
